      "content": "The feeling of being a hollow shell while others see a ghost of who you were is an agonizing weight to carry. That performance you describe is exhausting, and it is valid to feel that it's pointless. Instead of trying to force the old self back, perhaps the only honest thing is to allow yourself the grace to simply *not* be that person right now. You don't have to perform for anyone; you just have to be present for the next moment.",
